# Where a known landmark is right now, as seen by the robot's own sensors --
# for the last metre of a charge, where a dock pose from the map is not
# precise enough. Served by landmark_detector (the workspace's
# syncai_landmark_detection) on the relative name `detect_landmark` ->
# <robot_id>/detect_landmark. Called by the DetectLandmark BT node; the
# backend does not call it. New in 2026-11.
#
# THE DETECTOR ONLY DETECTS. It returns where the landmark is and how sure the
# sighting is; it never commands motion, never decides whether a sighting is
# good enough (thresholds on `consecutive` / `ambiguous` /
# `reprojection_error_px` are the caller's), and returns the landmark, not the
# dock: where the robot should stop relative to the landmark is the dock's
# geometry, the caller's too.
#
# A QUERY, NOT A TRIGGER. While active, the detector processes every frame
# (a plugin may need the history: ArUco's mirror ambiguity is resolved over
# several frames), and a call returns the newest sighting at once. It never
# waits for a frame, so the caller polls at its own rate. The first call wakes
# a detector in standby and answers SENSOR_STARTING; the detector goes back to
# standby after its idle_timeout without a call.
#
# `landmark_id` names an entry in the node's landmark registry (its params
# file), which names the detector plugin and the landmark's own parameters --
# for ArUco the dictionary, the marker id and the printed size. The caller
# never names the detection method. The printed size is the landmark's, not
# the detector's: two prints of different sizes under one detector-wide size
# give a wrong distance with no error.

# Registry name, e.g. "charger_a". Required.
string landmark_id
# Frame of the returned pose; empty -> the sensor's own frame, untransformed
# (the image's frame_id, <robot_id>/camera_optical_frame for the camera: z
# ahead, x right, y down). Empty is the default because it needs no TF and so
# answers in every mode: a detector that saw the landmark should never fail on
# a frame the caller did not ask for (until 2026-11-10 empty meant the node's
# odom_frame, which failed TRANSFORM_FAILED wherever lio_bridge was not
# running). A fixed frame for a docking target is the consumer's to choose:
# name it here, or transform the result with its stamp. Any other frame is
# transformed at the image stamp, not at the call: the robot moves between
# the capture and the call. Prefer odom (continuous) over map (jumps on a
# localizer correction).
string target_frame
# Oldest sighting accepted, seconds; <= 0 -> the node's default_max_age.
# Older than this is NOT_DETECTED, the last sighting's age in error_msg.
float32 max_age
---
# Retry = the same call may succeed later; permanent = it will not.
#
# Numbered locally, not in NavigateToGoal's 3xx docking range as DockToPose's
# are: detection is not docking-specific (any tree may look for a landmark),
# and the DetectLandmark BT node maps these to the tree's own failure.
uint16 NONE=0
uint16 UNKNOWN=1
# Permanent: landmark_id is not in the registry; error_msg lists the ones
# that are.
uint16 UNKNOWN_LANDMARK=2
# Retry: this call woke the detector, or it woke recently, and no frame has
# arrived yet.
uint16 SENSOR_STARTING=3
# Retry, but likely persistent: active, and the plugin cannot use its sensor
# -- no frame for the node's frame_timeout (the camera stream is down), or
# frames it cannot use: no camera_info or one for another resolution, a frame
# that does not decode or that the detection threw on. error_msg says which.
# A bad frame's reason is cleared by the next good one.
uint16 SENSOR_UNAVAILABLE=4
# Retry: frames arrive, no sighting newer than max_age -- or the newest is in
# an image stamped more than max_age ahead of the node's clock, so how old it
# is cannot be told (the camera's and the node's clocks disagree; error_msg
# says by how much).
uint16 NOT_DETECTED=5
# Retry: the sensor -> target_frame transform at the image stamp failed.
# Never with target_frame empty.
uint16 TRANSFORM_FAILED=6

uint16 error_code
# Detail for the log; empty when error_code is NONE.
string error_msg
# The landmark in target_frame, stamped with the image it was seen in. Origin
# at the landmark's centre, +x out of its face (towards a robot in front of
# it), +z up. 6-DOF: projecting it onto the floor is the caller's. Valid only
# with error_code NONE.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped pose
# Seconds from pose.header.stamp to the answer. Never negative: an image
# stamped ahead of the node's clock by up to max_age answers 0.
float32 age
# Sightings in a row behind this pose, this one included; reset by a frame
# without the landmark.
uint16 consecutive
# True while the plugin holds an alternative pose it has not ruled out
# (ArUco: the mirrored PnP solution, near the marker's axis at ~1 m). The pose
# is the plugin's best choice even then. Always false for a plugin with no
# such ambiguity.
bool ambiguous
# The plugin's fit residual in pixels (ArUco: the corners' reprojection
# error); -1 when the plugin has none. No covariance yet: none of the plugins
# can fill one honestly.
float32 reprojection_error_px
